      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "David is so old at this point that he can't even seem to retain any body heat. I assume he is very skinny here, and so there's no fat on his bones to keep him warm. They layered him with all sorts of jackets and thermals and skins and whatever they could get, and it just didn't seem to be sufficient for him. We have gotten the full scope of David's life, and it is interesting to view David in this context. We don't often think about the ending of David; we only think about the power and might of David, the young shepherd boy defeating a big giant. I'm thankful scripture gives the full scope of David's life because if it just ended in 2 Samuel with David's old age, we would be left on a bit of a cliffhanger, uncertain what would become of Israel now that they have a good king.",
