      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "\"Adonijah\" means \"My Lord is Jehovah.\" This is the fourth son of David. \"Haggith\" means \"Festive.\" Haggith isn't spoken about much. We know that David does get busy with marrying quite a few women in 2 Samuel, so she is just one on the list. This is why it's not a good idea to marry more than one woman. This fact continues to be a problem for David even into his old age. Adonijah was trying to take the authority upon himself to make the decision of who gets to be king of the throne without permission from anybody. This was a prideful motive here. He \"exalted\" himself.",
