      "startVerse": 17,
      "endVerse": 19,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "To make it very obvious to David, there was only one son of his who was not invited. David had about twenty kids (though only a few get some recognition, and it's usually for terrible reasons). Two are dead (not including Bathsheba's baby who passed away after birth), so that leaves about eighteen left. Seventeen go to this party, and Solomon is the odd man out. That seems pretty personal to me. Adonijah doesn't want Solomon as king. Honestly, I don't really think David wanted Solomon as king either. However, that is who the Lord chose, and so it will be the Lord's decision that gets the next king placed on the throne.",
